    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81194.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Yes, what an incredible year. It's really unusual and every weekend usually brings some dynamic news, although let's see, the weekend's not over yet. Well, I wasn't sure if she would actually stay in, but I think she will because she did secure the delegates this week and she did unleash a lot of the frozen funding that was not going to Joe Biden, that is now going to her now that she looks to be a certainty. Of course, that'll all be determined. when the delegates vote on August 19th at the Democrat Convention. So look, it's historic. It's going to be very interesting to see how she unravels her terrible record, the far left member of the Senate when she was there, left of Bernie Sanders, who's a self-proclaimed communist. So that is really worth noting. You see the scramble to try to erase the public record of her record. Obviously, a lot of media trying to take down that she wasn't really the borders are, that she wasn't, it wasn't her primary responsibility. You see that trying to take down her record and changing the way they do ratings so that she doesn't look like she's left of Bernie Sanders, which is really notable because in 2020 Bernie Sanders was leading in the polls and that's when the Democrats interfered in their own democratic process in their own primary process because their voters were supporting Bernie Sanders and they basically again forced Pete Buttigieg out, forced Amy Klobuchar out, and the two of them were tearfully out of the race on the same day, and all of a sudden that boosted Joe Biden, who was their preferred pick because they didn't want someone like Bernie Sanders, again, a self-proclaimed communist, you know, supporter of the Green New Deal, supporter of open borders, supporter of everything leftist, everything self, or authoritarian. And they wanted to have someone like Joe Biden, who has an image, not a record, but had an image of being a moderate. And then Joe Biden picked Kamala Harris. So when they forced them out, and here they are with someone worse than Bernie Sanders, if you look at a record. So now they've got to come around and focus on issues to try to boost her. But I think it's going to be very difficult for the Democrats to do this with the other. Yes, they're going to have a lot of money. They're going to portray You know, President Trump is some kind of diabolical monster, which they always do and they've always done. They're going to undermine our political process, you know, go after the Supreme Court, continue with lawfare, all that's going to happen. But I do think that they're going to have, you know, she's in her honeymoon period right now. I think It's going to start eroding as we move forward into her real record, getting out there, and there's going to be over a billion dollars spent on this race with only 400 days or more to go. A lot to look forward to, so I would say buckle up, it's going to be quite an interesting election year.",
