    "turn_text": "Well, we were watching it. I mean, I don't, maybe they cut some of it off, but it was certainly on social media while I was in the chamber listening to the speech you could see. A lot of the protesters out there, you know, on our social media feeds, whether it was like Instagram, Twitter, those types of things. So it was out there. I think a lot of the corporate media, maybe ABC, NBC, CBS, CNN, MSNBC were probably minimizing it, but I thought quite a bit on Fox Business, Fox News. And I think it's important. People should see they desecrated a flag. It was not a flag they own. We have free speech. If you want to buy your own flag and burn it, you can do that. Of course, it's offensive to people like me, who has a son who's serving in the military or others who really believe strongly in the symbol of our flag, which stands for freedom and human rights. But they took down flags that were owned by the federal government. You know, in front of Union Station, the train station, and they were burning those. So that's destruction of someone else's property. That's actually prohibited. They were also desecrating monuments, putting on Hamas's coming, death to America. These are Americans, I think, for the most part, doing this. These are people who are anti-American, driven by this, you know, just evil force that is Iran using Hamas, Hezbollah, and these, you know, organizations that are involved in terrorism.",
